---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for LuVicen Android apps published on Google Play"
  pubDate={new Date('August 07 2026')}
  heroImage="/logo.png"
>
  <p>
    At LuVicen we respect your privacy and believe transparency is essential to user trust. This privacy policy explains the data we collect, how we use it, and how we protect information related to the Android apps we develop and publish on Google Play.
  </p>

  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This policy applies to all mobile applications created by LuVicen and distributed through Google Play. It includes apps that may collect personal information, usage data, or technical device information.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>Depending on the app, LuVicen may collect the following types of information:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Information provided directly by the user, such as name, email address, or contact details.</li>
    <li>Technical device information, including device model, Android version, device identifiers, and performance data.</li>
    <li>App usage data, such as error reports, interaction events, and features used.</li>
    <li>Data required for specific app features, such as access to the camera, files, or location, only when the user grants explicit permission.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Purpose of Processing</h2>
  <p>We use the collected information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide, maintain, and improve the application.</li>
    <li>Fix bugs and ensure stable performance.</li>
    <li>Send notifications and app-related communications when the user authorizes it.</li>
    <li>Meet legal obligations and protect LuVicen's rights.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Consent and Google Play Permissions</h2>
  <p>
    All of our apps request permissions in a transparent way and only when they are necessary for functionality. Before accessing sensitive data, the user must accept each permission. This policy complies with Google Play requirements for privacy and data handling.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-Party Use and Providers</h2>
  <p>
    In some cases, we may use third-party services for analytics, hosting, or technical support. These providers may process data in a limited way and always under our protection standards. We do not sell or share your data with third parties for commercial purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not share users' personal information with external companies, except when:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>It is necessary to comply with a legal obligation.</li>
    <li>It is required to protect rights, safety, or property.</li>
    <li>The user has given explicit consent.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    LuVicen implements reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect information from unauthorized access, alteration, or destruction. However, no system is completely infallible, so we recommend users handle their data carefully.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We retain data only for as long as needed to fulfill its processing purpose, to handle support requests, or to comply with legal obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>User Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Users have the right to request information about the data LuVicen holds, to correct it, delete it, or restrict its use when applicable. They may also opt out of commercial communications or withdraw consent at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this privacy policy or wish to exercise your rights, contact us at:
  </p>
  <p>
    LuVicen<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:admin@luvicen.cl">admin@luvicen.cl</a><br />
    WhatsApp: <a href="https://wa.me/56984117366">+56 9 8411 7366</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Policy Changes</h2>
  <p>
    LuVicen may update this policy in the future. We will publish the latest version on this page and notify users if changes are relevant to their data or app usage.
  </p>
</Layout>
